// @trap :20:0
// THE UNMASKED FORM of `trap-message.vl` — `__trap__("reason")` as the ONLY
// statement in the program, with nothing that prints anywhere.
//
// `trap-message.vl` carries a trailing `print(x)` (to pin that the abort skips
// it), and on `367ab8d` that bystander was the ONLY thing holding the fixture
// up: `scanPrintUse` reserved the 4-import print family for `print` and for
// `__log__` but NOT for `__trap__(<string>)`, whose reason streams through the
// very same `__print_char__`/`__print_str_flush__` pair. Delete the print and
// the program reserved nothing, the module got no import section at all, the
// two streaming calls resolved to USER function indices, and `vl build` wrote a
// 351-byte module that could not instantiate — `vl check` rc 0 throughout.
//
// So the sibling file was not testing what its name says: it was testing
// `__trap__` PLUS a print. This file is the cell that was actually untested,
// and it is the one that fails without the `__trap__` arm in the import scan.
//
// The bare `__trap__()` (`trap.vl`) never needed the imports — it lowers to
// `unreachable` alone — which is why the defect was confined to the MESSAGE form.
__trap__("boom: nothing else in this program prints")
